# clickhouse-backup runtime config (optional overrides).
#
# Installed at /etc/rtl-scanner/clickhouse-backup.env by
# ops/clickhouse-backup/install.sh; both backup.sh and restore.sh read it via
# EnvironmentFile=- (the service) or by sourcing it (manual runs). All values
# below have sane defaults baked into backup.sh, so this file is optional.

# ── Where snapshots are written ──
# CRITICAL: point this at OFF-HOST storage. A backup on the same disk that is
# failing is not a backup. Good options:
#   - an external USB drive mounted at boot (/mnt/backup)
#   - a NAS / second machine over NFS or SMB
#   - an rclone-mounted cloud bucket
# Default (NOT off-host, fix this on a real deploy):
# BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/rf-clickhouse

# ── Which databases to back up ──
# Space-separated. Default covers the two pipelines with irreplaceable data.
# Add adsb/ais/ism only if those stacks actually run on this host.
# DATABASES=spectrum acars

# ── Snapshot retention (days) ──
# Snapshots older than this are pruned after each successful run.
# RETENTION_DAYS=14

# ── Per-database ClickHouse passwords ──
# Convention: user == db name, password == <db>_local. Override per db here if
# you hardened a password away from the committed dev default. Var name is the
# UPPERCASED db name + _PASSWORD.
# SPECTRUM_PASSWORD=spectrum_local
# ACARS_PASSWORD=acars_local
# NOAA_PASSWORD=noaa_local
